# Setuptools Best Practices

## Overview

Setuptools is the de facto standard for Python package development and distribution. This guide covers best practices for creating maintainable, distributable Python packages using modern setuptools configurations.

## Core Principles

- Use declarative configuration over imperative setup.py code
- Prefer pyproject.toml for modern Python packaging
- Include comprehensive metadata for package discovery
- Follow PEP standards for packaging (PEP 517, PEP 518, PEP 621)
- Implement proper dependency management
- Configure automated testing and distribution

## Package Structure

### Modern Project Layout

```
my_package/
├── pyproject.toml          # Modern build configuration
├── setup.cfg               # Legacy but still supported
├── setup.py                # Minimal shim for editable installs
├── README.md               # Project documentation
├── LICENSE                 # License file
├── MANIFEST.in             # Additional files to include
├── src/                    # Source layout (recommended)
│   └── my_package/
│       ├── __init__.py
│       ├── main.py
│       └── utils.py
├── tests/                  # Test directory
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── test_main.py
└── docs/                   # Documentation
```

## Configuration Examples

### Modern pyproject.toml Configuration

```toml
[build-system]
requires = ["setuptools>=61.0", "wheel"]
build-backend = "setuptools.build_meta"

[project]
name = "my-awesome-package"
version = "1.0.0"
description = "A comprehensive example package"
readme = "README.md"
license = {text = "MIT"}
authors = [
    {name = "Your Name", email = "you@example.com"},
]
maintainers = [
    {name = "Maintainer Name", email = "maintainer@example.com"},
]
classifiers = [
    "Development Status :: 5 - Production/Stable",
    "Intended Audience :: Developers",
    "License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License",
    "Programming Language :: Python :: 3",
    "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.8",
    "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.9",
    "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.10",
    "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.11",
    "Topic :: Software Development :: Libraries :: Python Modules",
]
requires-python = ">=3.8"
dependencies = [
    "requests>=2.28.0",
    "click>=8.0.0",
    "pydantic>=2.0.0",
]

[project.optional-dependencies]
dev = [
    "pytest>=7.0.0",
    "pytest-cov>=4.0.0",
    "black>=22.0.0",
    "mypy>=1.0.0",
    "ruff>=0.1.0",
]
docs = [
    "sphinx>=5.0.0",
    "sphinx-rtd-theme>=1.0.0",
]

[project.urls]
Homepage = "https://github.com/yourusername/my-package"
Documentation = "https://my-package.readthedocs.io"
Repository = "https://github.com/yourusername/my-package.git"
Issues = "https://github.com/yourusername/my-package/issues"

[project.scripts]
my-command = "my_package.main:cli"

[tool.setuptools]
package-dir = {"" = "src"}

[tool.setuptools.packages.find]
where = ["src"]
include = ["my_package*"]
exclude = ["tests*"]

[tool.setuptools.package-data]
my_package = ["data/*.json", "templates/*.html"]
```

### Entry Points Configuration

```toml
[project.entry-points."my_package.plugins"]
plugin1 = "my_package.plugins:Plugin1"
plugin2 = "my_package.plugins:Plugin2"

[project.entry-points.console_scripts]
my-cli = "my_package.cli:main"
my-tool = "my_package.tools:run"
```

### Minimal setup.py for Compatibility

```python
#!/usr/bin/env python
"""Minimal setup.py for backwards compatibility and editable installs."""
from setuptools import setup

if __name__ == "__main__":
    setup()
```

## Dependency Management

### Install Requirements

```toml
# Basic dependencies
dependencies = [
    "numpy>=1.20.0,<2.0.0",     # Version range
    "pandas~=1.3.0",            # Compatible release
    "requests[socks]>=2.28.0",  # With extras
    "click>=8.0.0",             # Minimum version
]

# Platform-specific dependencies
dependencies = [
    "pywin32>=300; sys_platform == 'win32'",
    "uvloop>=0.17.0; sys_platform != 'win32'",
]
```

### Development Dependencies

```python
# In setup.cfg or pyproject.toml
[options.extras_require]
dev = 
    pytest>=7.0.0
    pytest-cov>=4.0.0
    pytest-mock>=3.10.0
    black>=22.0.0
    flake8>=6.0.0
    mypy>=1.0.0
test = 
    pytest>=7.0.0
    pytest-cov>=4.0.0
docs = 
    sphinx>=5.0.0
    sphinx-rtd-theme>=1.0.0
all = 
    %(dev)s
    %(docs)s
```

## Version Management

### Dynamic Version from File

```toml
[project]
name = "my-package"
dynamic = ["version"]

[tool.setuptools.dynamic]
version = {attr = "my_package.__version__"}
```

### Version File (src/my_package/__init__.py)

```python
"""My Package - A comprehensive example."""
__version__ = "1.0.0"
__author__ = "Your Name"
__email__ = "you@example.com"

from .main import MyClass, my_function

__all__ = ["MyClass", "my_function", "__version__"]
```

## Package Discovery

### Automatic Package Finding

```python
# setup.cfg approach
[options]
packages = find:
package_dir = 
    = src

[options.packages.find]
where = src
include = my_package*
exclude = 
    tests
    tests.*
    docs
    docs.*
```

### Explicit Package Listing

```toml
[tool.setuptools]
packages = [
    "my_package",
    "my_package.submodule1",
    "my_package.submodule2",
    "my_package.utils",
]
```

## Data Files Inclusion

### MANIFEST.in Example

```text
# Include documentation
include README.md
include LICENSE
include CHANGELOG.md

# Include data files
recursive-include src/my_package/data *.json *.csv
recursive-include src/my_package/templates *.html *.jinja2

# Include test files in source distributions
recursive-include tests *.py *.json

# Exclude unnecessary files
global-exclude *.pyc
global-exclude __pycache__
global-exclude .DS_Store
prune .github
prune docs/_build
```

### Package Data Configuration

```toml
[tool.setuptools.package-data]
my_package = [
    "data/*.json",
    "data/*.csv", 
    "templates/*.html",
    "static/**/*",
]

[tool.setuptools.exclude-package-data]
"*" = [
    "tests/*",
    "*.pyc",
    "__pycache__/*",
]
```

## Build and Distribution

### Building Packages

```bash
# Install build tools
pip install --upgrade build twine

# Build source and wheel distributions
python -m build

# Check distribution files
twine check dist/*

# Upload to TestPyPI first
twine upload --repository testpypi dist/*

# Upload to PyPI
twine upload dist/*
```

### GitHub Actions for Automated Publishing

```yaml
name: Publish Package

on:
  release:
    types: [published]

jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
    - uses: actions/checkout@v3
    - name: Set up Python
      uses: actions/setup-python@v4
      with:
        python-version: '3.x'
    - name: Install dependencies
      run: |
        python -m pip install --upgrade pip
        pip install build twine
    - name: Build package
      run: python -m build
    - name: Publish to PyPI
      env:
        TWINE_USERNAME: __token__
        TWINE_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.PYPI_API_TOKEN }}
      run: twine upload dist/*
```

## Testing Configuration

### Pytest Integration

```toml
[tool.pytest.ini_options]
minversion = "7.0"
addopts = [
    "-ra",
    "--strict-markers",
    "--cov=my_package",
    "--cov-report=term-missing",
    "--cov-report=html",
]
testpaths = ["tests"]
python_files = ["test_*.py", "*_test.py"]
```

### Tox Configuration

```ini
[tox]
envlist = py{38,39,310,311}, lint, docs
isolated_build = True

[testenv]
deps = 
    pytest>=7.0.0
    pytest-cov>=4.0.0
commands = 
    pytest {posargs}

[testenv:lint]
deps = 
    black
    flake8
    mypy
commands = 
    black --check src tests
    flake8 src tests
    mypy src

[testenv:docs]
deps = 
    sphinx
    sphinx-rtd-theme
commands = 
    sphinx-build -W -b html docs docs/_build/html
```

## Best Practices

### Do's
- Always include comprehensive metadata
- Use semantic versioning (MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH)
- Pin dependencies appropriately
- Include classifiers for better discoverability
- Test package installation in clean environments
- Use src/ layout for better testing isolation
- Include type hints and py.typed marker
- Document all public APIs

### Don'ts
- Don't use setup.py for configuration (use pyproject.toml)
- Don't include test files in distributions (unless necessary)
- Don't use relative imports in packages
- Don't forget to update version numbers
- Don't include sensitive data in packages
- Don't use deprecated setuptools features

## Migration from setup.py

### Converting setup.py to pyproject.toml

```python
# Old setup.py
from setuptools import setup, find_packages

setup(
    name="my-package",
    version="1.0.0",
    packages=find_packages(),
    install_requires=[
        "requests>=2.28.0",
        "click>=8.0.0",
    ],
)
```

Becomes:

```toml
# New pyproject.toml
[build-system]
requires = ["setuptools>=61.0"]
build-backend = "setuptools.build_meta"

[project]
name = "my-package"
version = "1.0.0"
dependencies = [
    "requests>=2.28.0",
    "click>=8.0.0",
]
```

This comprehensive guide ensures proper package structure, configuration, and distribution practices for Python projects using setuptools.